AI-Powered Disaster Damage Assessment & Response Prioritization
1. Project Overview
We want to build an AI-powered web application that analyzes satellite imagery after natural disasters and helps emergency response teams identify and prioritize affected areas.
The system uses a pretrained Computer Vision model to detect and classify visible building damage.
It then divides the affected area into smaller zones and ranks them according to damage severity.
The goal is not only to identify damaged areas but also to help decision-makers understand which areas require attention first.
The system should support disasters such as earthquakes, floods, hurricanes, and wildfires.
Main Features:
AI-powered damage detection using satellite imagery.
Damage severity classification.
Before-and-after satellite image visualization.
Automatic division of affected areas into zones.
Intelligent zone priority ranking.
High, Medium, and Low priority classification.
Interactive dashboard with damage statistics.
Clear visual explanations of why each zone received its priority.
The first version should be a functional MVP, not a production-ready emergency response system.
We want to prioritize simplicity, actual AI inference, a polished interface, and reliable execution.
