3. Dataset
Dataset Name: xBD (xView2)
Official Dataset:
https://xview2.org/dataset
Official Baseline Repository:
https://github.com/DIUx-xView/xView2_baseline
xBD is a publicly available research dataset developed for building damage assessment using satellite imagery.
It contains real satellite images collected before and after natural disasters.
Dataset Contents
The dataset includes:
Pre-disaster satellite images.
Post-disaster satellite images.
Building location annotations.
Building damage classification labels.
Disaster metadata.
Geographic information for the annotated imagery.
The images are typically 1024 × 1024 pixels.
Damage Classes
The dataset provides four main damage categories:
Class Description
No Damage No visible building damage
Minor Damage Minor visible damage
Major Damage Significant visible damage
Destroyed Severe destruction
Some buildings may be marked as unclassified. These should be excluded from ground-truth evaluation.
How to Use the Dataset
For the MVP:
Download the dataset from the official website.
Registration may be required.
Select 2–3 image pairs showing different damage levels.
Use the matching pre-disaster and post-disaster images.
Keep their corresponding JSON annotations when available.
Do not download or process the entire dataset unless necessary.
We want a small dataset suitable for a fast demonstration.
The application must allow users to upload their own images or select local sample cases.
Do not assume the dataset files already exist.
If the dataset is unavailable, build the application and provide clear instructions for adding the required files.

