11. Important Implementation Requirements
Real AI inference is mandatory. The project must not be a UI-only demonstration.
Use the pretrained SegFormer-B0 checkpoint. Do not train a new model.
Make the implementation simple, understandable, and modular.
Do not use mock predictions in the actual analysis workflow.
Never describe ground-truth annotations as AI predictions.
Handle missing images and model download errors gracefully.
Cache the model to avoid downloading or loading it repeatedly.
Use lightweight dependencies wherever possible.
Keep all ranking formulas transparent and easy to modify.
Use the real model output to generate the damage statistics and priority rankings.
Do not invent geographic coordinates. The initial 3 × 3 zones are image-based sectors unless valid georeferencing information is available.
Avoid adding unnecessary features that could slow down development.
Keep dataset and model licenses in mind. The selected model is released under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.
Treat the prototype as a decision-support demonstration, not an operational emergency response system.
